{"name":"Camping Trip","hex":"#67786e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"camping","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of camp"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The recreational or educational activity of temporarily living in a tent or similar accommodation.","The act of setting up a camp."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/camping"},{"term":"trip","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A journey; an excursion or jaunt.","A short outing for a specified purpose."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fall over or stumble over an object as a result of striking it with one's foot","To cause (a person or animal) to fall or stumble by knocking their feet from under them."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Camping Trip (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Camping Trip is a 2022 Canadian crime thriller drama film written by Leonardo Fuica, directed by Leonardo Fuica and Demian Fuica and starring Leonardo Fuica, Caitlin Cameron, Alex Gravenstein and Hannah Forest Briand."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4b/Camping_Trip_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camping_Trip_(film)"},{"title":"Camping","blocks":[{"text":"Camping is a form of outdoor recreation or outdoor education involving overnight stays with a basic temporary shelter such as a tent. Camping can also include a recreational vehicle, sheltered cabins, a permanent tent, a shelter such as a bivy or tarp, hammock, or no shelter at all. Typically, participants leave developed areas to spend time outdoors, in pursuit of activities providing them enjoyment or in a form of educational experience. Spending the night away from home distinguishes camping from day-tripping, picnicking, and other outdoor activities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Tent_campin